---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { groups } from '../../../data/ruleGroups';
import { rulesOfGroup } from '../../../data/rulesIndex';
---

<Doc
  title="The forty rules"
  kicker="Track O — Own your Discipline"
  description="The 40 measurable OTAKU rules, grouped by pillar, with the thresholds and the primary metric."
  path="/guide/rules"
>
  <p class="lede">
    Forty rules, each with a threshold. They are mechanical for a reason: a rule that
    depends on taste cannot be reviewed, automated or argued with.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Cyclomatic complexity ≤ 5 per method</strong> is the primary metric. It
    counts the independent paths a reader must hold at once: each branch, loop and
    boolean operator adds one. The rest of the discipline exists to keep that number
    low. Every rule below has its own page with purpose, concept, problem and solution.
  </p>

  {groups.map((group) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{group.pillar} — {group.title.en}</h2>
      <ul class="rules-index">
        {rulesOfGroup(group.id).map((rule) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/guide/rules/${rule.slug}/`}>
              <span class="n">{String(rule.id).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              <span>{rule.title.en}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  ))}

  <p>
    When in doubt, choose the more restrictive option. That is the tie-breaker the
    philosophy prescribes.
  </p>
</Doc>
